  "changed_since_previous": "Dropped two commits from the previous revision (a mempool time representation refactor and link-time exclusion of `NodeClock::now()` from `libbitcoinkernel`, moved to a follow-up branch). Added `btck_chainstate_manager_options_set_clock_time` and adapted the `utxo_total_supply` fuzz target to use the per-chainman clock.",
  "card": "This pull request adds `btck_chainstate_manager_set_clock_time` and `btck_chainstate_manager_options_set_clock_time`, allowing kernel library consumers and tests to set validation time per `ChainstateManager` instance rather than globally. Validation time checks (header future-time checks, IBD status, and progress reporting) now call `ChainstateManager::Now()` instead of reading `NodeClock::now()` directly. This isolates concurrent chainstate managers from global clock modifications and fixes an intermittent test race across second boundaries. It has no open PR dependencies.",
